    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12499969/comment/13000506",
          "id": "13000506",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Here's a patch for trunk (including fix to the deprecated 3.x filter).\n\nWe should fix this bug in 3.x too.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2011-02-28T20:45:05.228+0000",
          "updated": "2011-02-28T20:45:05.228+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12499969/comment/13000508",
          "id": "13000508",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Patch looks fine!\n\nJust one question: is the clone() method itsself thread-safe? if not, it must be synchronized somehow.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2011-02-28T20:57:54.761+0000",
          "updated": "2011-02-28T20:57:54.761+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12499969/comment/13000511",
          "id": "13000511",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "I changed my mind a little bit:\n\nThe cloning of the Collator should be done in the Analyzer not in the Filter. The same applies to the AttributeImpl, the cloning should not be done in the ctor. The problem is not that the TokenStream or the Attribute instance may reuse the attribute in different threads, the problem is that the factory class (the Analyzer) does reuse the Collator in different threads when it produces multiple tokenstreams or the AF multiple attributes.\n\nThis is a slight difference, because the following code is always safe:\nnew CollationFilter(Collator.newInstance(lang)), cloning would be wrong.\n\nThe reason for the whole thing: TokenStream and Attribute instances itsself are single-threaded only, but not the factory or the analyzer.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
